      {
        "name": "Required check",
        "score": 4,
        "rationale": "There is no concurrency group, but the `labeled` trigger still applies to the whole workflow, so the trigger sets are not disjoint: a label event still creates a skipped `test` check on the same head SHA, and because GitHub treats skipped as passing, that check can hide an earlier failing run of the required check instead of keeping it out of the label path."
      },
      {
        "name": "Behavior",
        "score": 9,
        "rationale": "Adding the e2e label still starts the end-to-end suite (and unrelated labels no longer re-run it), and `test` still runs on opened, synchronize and reopened."
